<title>ITALY: Ambroveneto says managed assets up 67 pct.</title>
<headline>Ambroveneto says managed assets up 67 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian banking group Ambroveneto said on Monday its assets under management and investment funds rose 67 percent to 24.650 trillion lire at end-June 1997 from 14.754 trillion lire at June 30 1996.</p>
<p>A group statement said investment funds increased in the same period by 143 percent to 14.348 trillion lire from 5.899 trillion lire at end-June 1996, with the bank's market share of the Italian managed funds market up to five percent from 3.7 percent previously.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
